From: Lucas C.S. <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] build/config/compiler: rebase chromium-patches' cr152-compiler.patch onto M156

Rebase of chromium-patches-152 toolchain/cr152-compiler.patch (Matt Jolly,
2026-08-22), which drops the `clang_revision`, `rustc_revision` and
`compiler_cpu_abi` configs from `config("compiler")` along with the bundled-
toolchain consistency checks and absolute-path stripping that a system
LLVM/Rust cannot satisfy.

Only its third hunk needed work.  It deletes `config("clang_revision")`
outright, and M156 grew that config's Rust branch: the single rustc revision
assert became a loop that also checks the crubit and bindgen revisions in
//third_party/rust-toolchain/VERSION.  The hunk now deletes the M156 body;
the other thirteen hunks are byte-identical to the original in content, with
line numbers regenerated against the pristine 156.0.8078.47 file.

The ebuild applies this with the other files/ patches -- before the
patchset's llvm/ and toolchain/ directories -- so it is generated against the
pristine tree, and deletes the original from the unpacked patchset.  Drop it
when PATCH_V moves to a chromium-patches release that ships a cr156 (or
later) compiler patch.
